  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Flow Board",
    "overview": "Upflow is a board a team gathers around. The surface is black, white and gray, close to unstyled, so that the only color on screen is the state of the work: how long a PR has been open, how big it is, whether it is waiting on someone. A manager, a developer and a consultant should be able to look at the same screen and point at the same red dot.\n\nThe system is dense and calm. Lists, rows of small round blocks, a few stat cards, and plain headings carry everything. There is no decorative imagery, gradient or brand illustration; the incumbent UI is shadcn/ui (new-york, neutral base) on Tailwind v4, and new screens extend it rather than restyle it.\n\nA brand accent color is wanted but not yet chosen. Until it is, nothing on the surface uses color for identity.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Monochrome chrome, chromatic data.",
      "System sans at small sizes; hierarchy from weight and size, not color.",
      "Flat surfaces separated by hairline borders.",
      "Round blocks as the unit of work: one block is one PR.",
      "Every hidden or filtered item is counted and stated on screen."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Color Means Data Rule",
        "body": "Chrome (buttons, headings, navigation, cards) stays in the neutral ramp. A hue on screen must answer \"what state is this PR in?\" If it doesn't, it is gray.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Accent Is Undecided Rule",
        "body": "A single brand accent is planned but not chosen. Do not introduce one inside a feature; propose it as its own change.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Numbers Align Rule",
        "body": "Counts that change or sit in a column use tabular figures (`tabular-nums`), so a count of 8 and a count of 23 line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Over Shadow Rule",
        "body": "To separate two areas, draw a 1px Hairline border. Don't add a shadow to a card, row or section.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep chrome in the neutral ramp and let only data carry hue (The Color Means Data Rule).",
      "Do reuse the age and size scales exactly as defined, with the same thresholds, wherever PR age or size appears.",
      "Do use Lucide icons at 14–16px; the filter icon (`list-filter`) marks filtering controls.",
      "Do write `dark:` variants for new color classes, as existing components do. Dark mode has no switch yet, but it is kept working.",
      "Do write UI copy in English. Japanese appears only as data until i18n lands.",
      "Do show counts with `tabular-nums` and say how many items are hidden and why."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce a brand accent, gradient or decorative color inside a feature.",
      "Don't give a new meaning to an existing data color (for example, using red for \"selected\").",
      "Don't add shadows to cards, rows or sections.",
      "Don't use emoji or text glyphs as new icons; the existing ✓ ✗ 💬 ⏳ marks are legacy, not a pattern to extend.",
      "Don't mix Japanese and English UI copy on one screen."
    ]
  }
}
